# Secrets must never enter an image layer. `COPY . .` would otherwise bake the
# local .env — SUPABASE_JWT_SECRET, DATABASE_URL, service-role keys — into the
# image, where anyone who can pull it (or read the registry) can extract it.
# Runtime config comes from compose `environment:` / the host, not from a file
# committed into the build context.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Host node_modules are built for the host OS/arch. Copying them over the
# `npm ci` output can shadow correct linux-musl binaries with Windows/macOS
# ones and produce native-module failures that only appear in the container.
node_modules
npm-debug.log*

# Build/dev noise that only inflates image size and cache invalidation.
.git
.gitignore
Dockerfile
.dockerignore
*.md
logs
*.log
coverage
.nyc_output
tests
.vscode
.idea
.DS_Store
